{"version": 3, "term": {"cols": 110, "rows": 32}, "timestamp": 1795649628, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "title": "Reliaburger 0.3.2: an agent sets up a cluster"}
[0.059, "m", "The prompt"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# One line from the homepage, given to Claude Code with a shell and an empty\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# RELIABURGER_HOME. It reads the playbook on reliaburger.com/agents and does the rest.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# Every line below is the real session as it ran. Idle time is cut to 2 s, and each slow step says how long it really took.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m» The prompt\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mSet up a Reliaburger cluster for me. Start at https://reliaburger.com/agents.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.523, "o", "\u001b[2m# Claude Code, model claude-fable-5-2\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.333, "m", "Read the playbook"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m» Read the playbook\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[1mfetch\u001b[0m https://reliaburger.com/agents\r\n"]
[7.296, "o", "\u001b[2mI can't reproduce the full page verbatim, but here's a concise summary of \"Working with an AI agent,\" the R…\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m**What it covers**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mReliaburger is a container orchestrator shipped as one binary. Its CLI, `relish`, includes an `relish agent…\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m**Key guidance for agents**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 21 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.18, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p /tmp/rb-page && curl -sL -A \"curl\" https://reliaburger.com/agents -o /tmp/rb-page/agents.html; wc\r\n  -c /tmp/rb-page/agents.html; sed -e 's/<script[^>]*>.*<\\/script>//g' -e 's/<[^>]*>//g'\r\n  /tmp/rb-page/agents.html | grep -v '^\\s*$' | grep -n -i -A200 'set up a cluster\\|setting up a\r\n  cluster\\|playbook' | head -300; which relish docker; uname -m\r\n"]
[0.7, "o", "\u001b[2m   99995 /tmp/rb-page/agents.html\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m19:0.2.7 as the commands arrive. It ends with the playbook an agent follows to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m20-set a cluster up for you, which is where reliaburger.com/agents sends one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m21-Add it to your agent #\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m22-Each button adds one MCP server, reliaburger, that runs relish mcp: read-only tools over stdio, with no …\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m23-Add to CursorAdd to VS CodeAdd to Goose\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m24-Claude Code, from a shell:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m25-claude mcp add reliaburger -- relish mcp\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 296 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.013, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m sed -e 's/<script[^>]*>.*<\\/script>//g' -e 's/<[^>]*>//g' /tmp/rb-page/agents.html | grep -v '^\\s*$' | sed\r\n  -n '1006,1100p'; which limactl qemu-system-aarch64; sysctl -n hw.memsize; vm_stat | head -5; df -h ~ | tail\r\n  -1\r\n"]
[0.059, "o", "\u001b[2mIt ends, so say when.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mHetzner and DigitalOcean have no free machines: pick the smallest with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m2 vCPUs and 2 GiB, and quote its price.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mOpen TCP 9117 to your human's address only, and the cluster ports between the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mmachines (the reference chapter lists them), in the provider's firewall.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mEvery one of these CLIs takes a user-data file when it creates a machine. Give\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2meach machine this one, with your human's public key:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m#cloud-config\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 87 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.435, "m", "Install and build"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m» Install and build\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m mkdir -p /tmp/rb-install && curl -fsSL https://reliaburger.com/install.sh -o /tmp/rb-install/install.sh &&\r\n  wc -l /tmp/rb-install/install.sh && cat /tmp/rb-install/install.sh; limactl list 2>&1 | head\r\n"]
[0.345, "o", "\u001b[2m     182 /tmp/rb-install/install.sh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m#!/bin/sh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# Reliaburger bootstrap. HTTPS authenticates the versioned installer; that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# installer pins the CLI checksum, and Relish verifies signed guest binaries.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# POSIX sh, so `curl -fsSL https://reliaburger.com/install.sh | sh -s -- --laptop`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# works with dash, bash, zsh and busybox alike. Installer options go after\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# `sh -s --`; with none, it explains the choices and downloads nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m#\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 182 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.057, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m cd /tmp/rb-install && curl -fsSL\r\n  https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/releases/download/v0.3.2/install.sh -o versioned.sh && wc -l\r\n  versioned.sh && grep -n -i 'install_dir\\|bin\\b\\|/bin\\|sudo\\|PATH\\|sha256\\|profile\\|rc\\b' versioned.sh | head\r\n  -60; ls ~/.reliaburger ~/.local/bin 2>&1 | head -30\r\n"]
[0.417, "o", "\u001b[2m     363 versioned.sh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m1:#!/bin/sh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m16:#   --no-modify-path   touch nothing outside ~/.reliaburger (also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m17:#                      RELIABURGER_NO_MODIFY_PATH=1)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m24:  if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m25:    sha256sum \"$1\" | awk '{print $1}'\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m97:  sysctl_command=$(command -v sysctl 2>/dev/null) || sysctl_command=/usr/sbin/sysctl\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m121:                  Ubuntu or Debian, and passwordless sudo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 61 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.601, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m sh /tmp/rb-install/install.sh --install-only 2>&1 | tail -20; export PATH=\"$HOME/.reliaburger/bin:$PATH\";\r\n  relish agent version; ls -la ~/.reliaburger ~/.reliaburger/dev | head -30; relish setup --help 2>&1 | head\r\n  -50\r\n"]
[3.271, "o", "\u001b[2mDownloading the Reliaburger v0.3.2 installer...\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mDownloaded 14823 bytes (14.5 KiB) in 0 s\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mDownloading relish v0.3.2 for macos-aarch64 (104.7 MiB)...\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mDownloaded 109738160 bytes (104.7 MiB) in 3 s\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mInstalled Relish v0.3.2 in /Users/miko/rbrec/bin\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mrelish is not on your PATH yet. Add this line to /Users/miko/.zshrc:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 19 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.507, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m echo \"RELIABURGER_HOME=$RELIABURGER_HOME\"; env | grep -i '^RELIA' | sed 's/TOKEN=.*/TOKEN=<set>/'; ls -la\r\n  ~/rbrec ~/rbrec/bin; R=~/rbrec/bin/relish; $R agent version; $R agent context; $R setup --help 2>&1 | head\r\n  -40\r\n"]
[0.071, "o", "\u001b[2mRELIABURGER_HOME=/Users/miko/rbrec\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mRELIABURGER_HOME=/Users/miko/rbrec\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m/Users/miko/rbrec:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mtotal 0\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mdrwx------    3 miko  staff    96 Nov 25 23:34 .\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mdrwxr-x---+ 101 miko  staff  3232 Nov 25 23:34 ..\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mdrwx------    3 miko  staff    96 Nov 25 23:34 bin\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 47 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.681, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The `relish` CLI is installed (v0.3.2), and the next step is your decision: where should the cluster\r\n         run?\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | Option | What it needs | Cost |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m |---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **1. This computer** (my recommendation) | Three Linux VMs in Lima, about 8 GiB of free memory and\r\n         15 GiB of disk | Free |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **2. Machines you already have, over SSH** | Ubuntu 24.04 or Debian 12+, 2 cores, 2 GiB memory, 10\r\n         GiB free under `/var/lib`, key-based SSH with passwordless sudo, and TCP 9117 on the first one\r\n         reachable from here | Free |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **3. A cloud** | New machines made with your logged-in provider CLI (`gcloud`, `oci`, `hcloud`,\r\n         `doctl` or `aws`) | I'd quote the monthly price first and create nothing paid without your yes |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **4. Spare machines with nothing on them** | UEFI network boot, Secure Boot off, 2 GiB memory, an 8\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         GB disk and a wired NIC | Free, but their disks are erased and you run the hands-on netboot and claim\r\n         steps |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m One machine is enough to try it; three form a council that survives losing one.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m What I found on this Mac that bears on option 1:\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **It qualifies:** Apple silicon, Lima installed, 32 GB of memory and 44 GiB of disk free.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Memory may be tight:** two Lima VMs are already running (`rb-bench-1030` and `reliaburger-test`,\r\n         8 GiB each). If setup struggles, stopping one of those would be the fix, and I won't touch them\r\n         without asking.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Your existing setup is untouched:** this session has `RELIABURGER_HOME=/Users/miko/rbrec`, so the\r\n         installer put `relish` in `/Users/miko/rbrec/bin`. Nothing in `~/.reliaburger` (your existing context\r\n         and keys) was changed, and a new cluster's credentials would also go under `~/rbrec`.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Nothing is on port 9117:** no cluster is answering there, so the default API port is free.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **`relish` is not on your PATH:** the installer left `~/.zshrc` alone. To add it yourself: `export\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         PATH=\"/Users/miko/rbrec/bin:$PATH\"`.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m I read the installer script before running it: it downloads the release from GitHub and checks the\r\n         binary's checksum.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m Reply with a number (and the `user@host` list for option 2, or the provider for option 3). For option\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         1, I'll run `relish setup --quickstart -o json`, then take you through the five-minute tour and leave\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         a summary with the teardown command.\r\n"]
