[31.1, "o", "\u001b[2mcluster: HEALTHY, no problems (rb-19f4696e9bd7-1 answered at 23:44:32 UTC)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mnodes      3 alive, 0 suspect, 0 dead\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mcouncil    leader rb-19f4696e9bd7-1 (term 1), 3/3 voters, quorum ok, 0 lagging\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mgossip     3 members, last change 38 s ago, 313 updates received\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mversions   bun v0.3.2 on 3 nodes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mcapacity   cpu 6% allocated (0 of 4 cores), memory 3%\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2musage      cpu 4% (busiest rb-19f4696e9bd7-1 7%), memory 29%, disk 38%; newest sample 3 s old\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# that took 31 s; the recording cut the wait\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.603, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m Your Reliaburger cluster is running on this Mac: three nodes on v0.3.2, status `HEALTHY, no\r\n         problems`, and `relish verify` confirmed every node runs the published release byte for byte.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m ## The cluster\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | | |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m |---|---|\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Where** | Three Lima VMs on this computer, cluster name `laptop` |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Nodes** | `rb-19f4696e9bd7-1` (leader), `-2`, `-3` |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **API** | `https://127.0.0.1:19117` |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **App address** | `http://localhost:18080` (the demo burger is at http://burger.localhost:18080) |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Admin credential** | `/Users/miko/rbrec/context.json` |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Back up** | The root CA backup `/Users/miko/rbrec/clusters/laptop/security/root-ca-backup.age`\r\n         and its identity `/Users/miko/rbrec/root-backup-keys/root-8315aa0ee0c90fc4.age-identity` |\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Cost** | Nothing per month; it uses about 11 GB of disk under `~/rbrec` |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m | **Remove it** | `/Users/miko/rbrec/bin/relish local destroy --name laptop --yes`, then `relish\r\n         uninstall` to remove the CLI and image cache |\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m Setup took 131 seconds and reported no warnings. Your existing `~/.reliaburger` and your other Lima\r\n         VMs were not touched.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m ## What the tour showed\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m I ran the five-minute tour against the demo app, and every step behaved as the manual describes:\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Build and deploy:** `burger:v1` was built on a node and deployed as eight apps from one image.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Batch:** 10 of 10 patty-cooking tasks succeeded.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Rolling deploy:** cheese went from v1 to v2 one replica at a time.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Automatic rollback:** the deliberately broken patty v3 failed its health check and the cluster\r\n         put v1 back and marked it `RolloutFailed`.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Agent proposal:** an agent token proposed scaling patty to 2, I approved it as admin, then undid\r\n         it. I revoked that token afterwards; only `laptop-admin` remains.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Policy test:** the example platform policies would deny the burger's images (they aren't from\r\n         `registry.example.com`), tested offline without applying anything.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m"]
[0.0, "o", " - **Faults:** a partition removed the lettuce for 30 seconds, a killed patty was restarted within\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         seconds, and a 300 ms delay showed up as `DEGRADED` in `relish path`.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Losing a node:** with node 3 stopped, the counters were rescheduled onto the other two nodes; I\r\n         started it again and the cluster returned to healthy.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m I shortened the delay fault from two minutes to 30 seconds and skipped `relish dashboard`, which is\r\n         interactive. No faults are active now.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m ## What's left running\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The burger demo is still deployed (9 apps, 14 instances), with a `diner` app ordering twice a second.\r\n         The demo source and `platform.toml` are in `~/rbrec/tour`.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m ## Next steps for you\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Put `relish` on your PATH:** add `export PATH=\"/Users/miko/rbrec/bin:$PATH\"` to `~/.zshrc`. It\r\n         only finds this cluster while `RELIABURGER_HOME=/Users/miko/rbrec` is set, as it is in this session.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Give future agent sessions a read-only token:** `relish token create --name agent --role read-\r\n         only --ttl-days 1`, passed as `RELIABURGER_TOKEN`, rather than the admin credential.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Wire Reliaburger into your agent clients:** `relish agent setup` shows the change and writes\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         nothing until you add `--yes`.\r\n"]
[0.316, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# The session ended after 19 turns and 10 m 50 s.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.0, "m", "You check"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1m» You check\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# You now, at your own prompt: is there a cluster?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m "]
